# NMDpredictionmodel: Guided Reproducibility Pipeline

This notebook provides a single entry point for running the annotation,
feature-generation, and TrunCat model-preparation workflow.

The notebook calls the scripts contained in this repository rather than
reimplementing their analysis logic.

## Supported datasets

- TOPMed
- gnomAD
- ClinVar
- GREGoR

## Important data-access note

Some source datasets, including TOPMed, are controlled-access and are not
distributed with this repository. Users must provide authorized copies of
controlled-access inputs.

Public reference datasets may either be downloaded manually or supplied
through the paths configured below.

## Main stages

1. Clone repository
2. Install dependencies
3. Configure dataset and reference paths
4. Run shared annotation
5. Run shared filtering
6. Run feature modules
7. Build the core feature table
8. For TOPMed, prepare the TrunCat model inputs
9. Run TrunCat model preprocessing and training
